<section class="panel overview-explanation"><h2>Support routes</h2><p><strong>Platform, account and privacy requests:</strong> <a href="mailto:<?=platform_directory_escape($data['email'])?>"><?=platform_directory_escape($data['email'])?></a>. Opening this address starts your email application; this dashboard sends no messages.</p><p><strong>Service bookings, quotes and invoices:</strong> direct the requester to the business named on its published website or document. FaraiOS does not confirm or change a service booking on that business’s behalf.</p><p><a href="../contact.html">Published contact guidance</a> · <a href="../privacy.html#export">Data export procedure</a> · <a href="../privacy.html#closure">Account closure procedure</a></p></section>
<section aria-label="Support coverage" class="stats overview-stages"><article><span>Responsible operator</span><strong style="font-size:1.2rem"><?=platform_directory_escape($data['operator'])?></strong><small>Sole operator · no backup operator assigned</small></article><article><span>Normal acknowledgement</span><strong style="font-size:1.2rem"><?=platform_directory_escape($data['normal'])?></strong><small>Acknowledgement, not resolution</small></article><article><span>Critical acknowledgement</span><strong style="font-size:1.2rem"><?=platform_directory_escape($data['critical'])?></strong><small>During covered operating hours</small></article></section>
<section class="panel overview-explanation"><h2>Operating hours and escalation</h2><p><strong><?=platform_directory_escape($data['hours'])?></strong> · <?=platform_directory_escape($data['timezone'])?>.</p><p>Outside these hours, support is best effort. This is not 24/7 coverage. Acknowledging a request does not mean the request, export or recovery has been completed.</p><p>For a suspected security incident, platform outage or risk to data, notify the responsible operator through the platform support route. Record the affected function, time and safe reproduction details; review <a href="platform-monitoring-page.php">Monitoring</a> and the <a href="platform.php?task=V1-014">incident and recovery procedure</a>. Do not copy credentials, confidential document links or customer message bodies into general tasks.</p><p>Confirm authority and scope before taking any incident action. If provider assistance is required, use the established provider support route and disclose only necessary, reviewed information. No automatic escalation or provider contact happens here.</p></section>
<section class="panel overview-explanation" aria-labelledby="support-cases"><h2 id="support-cases">Case status unavailable</h2><p><strong>No authorized support case feed is connected to this page.</strong> The confirmed route is the manual email process in the published contact and privacy guidance. Inbox access and ticket integration have not been established for this dashboard.</p><p>Open case count, case reference, category/status, age and assigned operator are <strong>unknown</strong>. This is not an empty queue or a statement that there are zero requests. No case freshness timestamp is available.</p><p>Future case visibility must use a reviewed source and authorization contract. Limit displayed fields to reference, category, status, age and responsible operator where permitted. Customer content, email addresses, attachments, credentials and private document tokens are excluded. No destination links are generated from untrusted case content.</p></section>
<section class="panel overview-explanation"><h2>Operator checklist</h2><details><summary>Data export requests</summary><ol><li>Verify the requester’s identity and authority. A business name, email address, booking reference or confidential link alone is not proof.</li><li>Agree the business, records, period and recipient. Review other people’s information; exclude credentials, private-link tokens and other businesses’ records.</li><li>Give a request reference and expected next update through the established manual process. Prepare and check completeness within the agreed scope.</li><li>Arrange private delivery to the verified recipient. Record the outcome and omissions; never place an export on a public website.</li></ol></details><details><summary>Closure and deletion requests</summary><ol><li>Verify identity and authority, clarify whether the request is unpublishing, access restriction, closure or deletion, and offer an export before changes.</li><li>Review open work, unpaid invoices, staff access, confidential links and scheduled communications with the authorized business owner.</li><li>Agree timing, records to retain, reasons and review dates. Do not affect another business or automatically erase financial and audit history.</li><li>Confirm completed actions and remaining restrictions. Do not mark closure complete while an agreed access or communication check remains unresolved. Deletion and waitlist withdrawal are separate processes.</li></ol></details><p>This page provides guidance only. It cannot export data, edit accounts, close cases, revoke access, delete records or send customer messages.</p></section>
<section class="panel overview-explanation"><h2>Sources and freshness</h2><p>Published <a href="../contact.html">contact guidance</a> and <a href="../privacy.html">privacy notice</a> checked <?=platform_directory_escape($data['policy_checked'])?>. This is a recorded policy check, not a live inbox refresh or delivery test. Recheck the linked procedure if policy changes.</p><p><a href="platform.php?task=V1-015">V1-015 privacy and lifecycle acceptance</a> · <a href="platform.php?task=TASK-405349EFBE">OWNER-10 delivery evidence</a>. Backup cadence verification remains separate.</p></section>
